From 4e9e5e5235d7351458a2747d2e5e0cef3964b667 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 15:19:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-71: each event lists ONLY the C++ function that
 runs; a double-click opens it (0.71.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EastSun 20260930 (on main.html's Exit OnClick, which listed the web sender,
control.acquire / release dispatches, MainClose.cpp, comment mentions, uses
and BCB6): "我需要你只對應到 W906_Main_CloseProgramOp，其他的事件也都是一樣".
- the events table: under each event ONE code row -- the function the port
  runs (the handler the command's dispatch calls, not a guard / lock / log
  helper around it; else the port's own live definition; else the server's
  form.event table row). Everything else found (the page's sender, the
  dispatch line, BCB6, mentions) is folded under 「其他找到的地方（n）」.
  A .dfm name that differs is shown as "sbCloseProgramClick -> W906_Main_
  CloseProgramOp". No function that runs -> says so; the C++ chip is dark.
- a double-click opens that function at once (no list to pick from).
- vscode_it.ps1: a page changed on disk while the test saved nothing is
  another session's when the extension has no way to write a file itself
  (no fs write / WorkspaceEdit delete or rename in extension.js or lib\) --
  a WARN with its uncommitted diff size, not a FAIL (20260930 15:12 another
  session added the Mot_Table button to HW.MotorTest.html mid-sweep). The
  IO page's tab is brought back in its own group (openWith without a column
  opened a second designer), and the Alias revert waits for the document.

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 154, smoke 156, panels, real VS Code 146):
real VS Code (sbCloseProgram OnClick -> W906_Main_CloseProgramOp in
MainClose.cpp and a double-click lands on MainClose.cpp:1318; BtnPanelLane3
OnClick -> W906_DispatchIoClick), panels (at most one code row under each
event, the rest folded), smoke (a new handler is the row's function).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
